Explanation of what this does:

1. We introduce a simple regex (`literalArgsPattern`) that looks for a pipe followed by one or more colon-separated string or numeric literals.
2. If it matches, we simply re-emit the raw `part` (via `replaceEndOfLine`) so that the original, tight 😄 `:` formatting is kept.
3. Otherwise we fall through into the existing Prettier-based formatting logic (which will add spaces around `:` for more complex cases, e.g. identifier arguments).

This change fixes the “always add spaces around `:` in pipes” regression in simple literal cases while preserving the previous behavior for everything else.
